<symbol type="2" id="26" code="202" name="Cliff"><description>A passable cliff or quarry. If the direction of fall of the cliff is not apparent from the contours, or to improve legibility, short tags may be drawn in the direction of the downslope.
For non-vertical cliffs, the tags should be drawn to show the full horizontal extent. Ends of the base line must be rounded if no tags appear. A passage between two cliffs must be at least 0.2 mm. A cliff should interplay with the contour lines.
Crossing a cliff will normally slow progress.
Minimum height: 1 m.
Minimum length: 0.6 mm (footprint 9 m).</description><line_symbol color="2" line_width="375" minimum_length="900" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="6000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="6000" break_length="1500" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="750" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol>
